# Code owners
#
# This project is one maintainer's, so the catch-all below is the whole policy
# and the explicit entries exist to say which files must never move without
# someone deliberately deciding they should. A change to any of them alters
# what production runs rather than how the code reads, so they are named here
# instead of left to the catch-all.

*                       @Dawe583

# Dependency resolution. The lockfile is the record of exactly which versions
# were reviewed, and a hand-edited entry in it is a dependency change that no
# manifest records.
pnpm-lock.yaml          @Dawe583

# The workspace root: scripts every gate in CI runs, the packageManager pin,
# the engines floor and the runtime dependency set.
/package.json           @Dawe583

# Deployment manifests. Each of these is read by the platform that runs the
# product rather than by NOMO, so a change here changes production without
# failing a test that could notice.
/vercel.json            @Dawe583
/server.json            @Dawe583
/Dockerfile             @Dawe583
/nitro.config.ts        @Dawe583

# The hosted function's deployment input. Appwrite receives a tarball, not a
# checkout, so this snapshot is what a deployed function serves in place of the
# source tree it was generated from. The GitHub gate fails rather than
# regenerating it, which is the point of naming it here as well.
/apps/appwrite-mcp/src/appwrite_mcp/nomo_snapshot.json   @Dawe583

# Database schema. Applied in order and never edited in place, because the
# ledger and the account tables underneath it are the production record of
# accountable tool calls.
/cloud/schema.sql       @Dawe583
/cloud/0001-account-ownership.sql                 @Dawe583
/cloud/0002-immutable-function-search-path.sql    @Dawe583

# The reversibility registry's policy source. The decisions it makes are what
# an intercepted tool call is answered with, so a change is a change to
# product behaviour under the name of configuration.
/policy/                @Dawe583
